// Clue Name :
"P2224120311" "Monument Records"
// DetailString :
"P3404344315" "You recorded these photos and measurements of the monument on the Bastion of Pain for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimPain 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2879249714" "The Verse of Pain"
// DetailString :
"P1765940607" "Justin Augustine's translation of the writing on the monumnt of Pain reads: <br><br>'And the Kind One was made prisoner within his Chantry,<br>And the Rularuu beset him in unending siege, <br>And Faathim the Kind knew only anguish, <br>For all his plans were cast down in ruin.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - DenialRecord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P575198989" "You recorded these photos and measurements of the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimDenial 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P499649486" "The Verse of Denial"
// DetailString :
"P292241210" "Justin Augustine's translation of the writing on the monumnt of Denial reads: <br><br>'And Faathim formed the Chantry from the very air, <br>And Faathim alone was master of it, <br>And within the Chantry Faathim stood shielded from Rularuu's will, <br>Here Faathim schemed for his freedom and his oblivion.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - GuiltRecord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2981331061" "You recorded these photos and measurements of the monument on the Bastion of Guilt for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimGuilt 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2882031593" "The Verse of Guilt"
// DetailString :
"P2571966356" "Justin Augustine's translation of the writing on the monumnt of Guilt reads: <br><br>'And when the world was split the Strong one Remained Loyal, <br>And the Strong one called Faathim Traitor for his plans, <br>And the Strong One called Faathim Traitor for his actions, <br>For Strength would let none stray from Rularuu.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimsList 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1641213704" "An Engraved Tablet"
// DetailString :
"P1342785542" "This stone tablet has been engraved in what looks like a series of ever more complex languages by Faathim the Kind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - BoydsRecordings 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P60385502" "Monuments around Zulu"
// DetailString :
"P4225103196" "You gathered these images and measurements of the monuments in the Firebase Zulu area for Dr. Bruce Boyd. With the knowledge gained by Justin Augustine, they may yeild new information."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimOldStory 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P221278516" "An old verse"
// DetailString :
"P2344654429" "Dr. Boyd's translations of the monuments found in the area around Firebase Zulu yeilded the following ominous verse: <br><br>'And give over your strong to Ruladak that he may work them, <br>And give over your injuries to Faathim that he may heal them, <br>And give over your outcast to Lanaru that he may execute them, <br>For you will know that they are Rularuu and are to be obeyed.' "

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ShameRecord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2338036960" "You recorded these photos and measurements of the monument on the Bastion of Shame for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimShame 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1011891615" "The Verse of Shame"
// DetailString :
"P2805954227" "Justin Augustine's translation of the writing on the monumnt of Shame reads: <br><br>'And by word and trickery the Traitor Faathim's work was done, <br>And the Mad One rose up with rage to split the world asunder, <br>And the Rularuu lost their truth and the People their master, <br>For Faathim's betrayal hid all from Rularuu's power.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SorrowRecord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2743362991" "You recorded these photos and measurements of the monument on the Bastion of Sorrow for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimSorrow 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2676672101" "The Verse of Sorrow"
// DetailString :
"P1720524324" "Justin Augustine's translation of the writing on the monumnt of Sorrow reads: <br><br>'And Kindness and Strength shook the the world with battle, <br>And by clever stratagem Strength was caught and bound, <br>And Kindness was was trapped as well within its fortress, <br>While Madness burned with rage and battled all.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - RegretRecord 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2812533255" "You recorded these photos and measurements of the monument on the Bastion of Regret for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - FaathimRegret 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P383524944" "The Verse of Regret"
// DetailString :
"P2456583592" "Justin Augustine's translation of the writing on the monumnt of Regret reads: <br><br>'And Kindness knew there would be freedom, <br>And Kindness knew that Rularuu could not be overthrown, <br>And Kindness new there would be no defiant haven of its hopes, <br>For now Kindness knew it would forever be of Rularuu.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - SagaOfFaathim 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P4064213771" "The Saga of Faathim"
// DetailString :
"P2677326679" "When the translations of the monuments surrounding the Chantry were done, Faathim the Kind put them in their proper order and recited them to you: <br><br>'And give over your strong to Ruladak that he may work them, <br>And give over your injuries to Faathim that he may heal them, <br>And give over your outcast to Lanaru that he may execute them, <br>For you will know that they are Rularuu and are to be obeyed. <br><br>And Faathim formed the Chantry from the very air, <br>And Faathim alone was master of it, <br>And within the Chantry Faathim stood shielded from Rularuu's will, <br>Here Faathim schemed for his freedom and his oblivion. <br><br>And by word and trickery the Traitor Faathim's work was done, <br>And the Mad One rose up with rage to split the world asunder, <br>And the Rularuu lost their truth and the People their master, <br>For Faathim's betrayal hid all from Rularuu's power. <br><br>And when the world was split the Strong one Remained Loyal, <br>And the Strong one called Faathim Traitor for his plans, <br>And the Strong One called Faathim Traitor for his actions, <br>For Strength would let none stray from Rularuu. 'And Kindness and Strength shook the the world with battle, <br>And by clever stratagem Strength was caught and bound, <br>And Kindness was was trapped as well within it's fortress, <br>While Madness burned with rage and battled all. <br><br>And the Kind One was made prisoner within his Chantry,<br>And the Rularuu beset him in unending siege, <br>And Faathim the Kind knew only anguish, <br>For all his plans were cast down in ruin. <br><br>And Kindness knew there would be freedom, <br>And Kindness knew that Rularuu could not be overthrown, <br>And Kindness new there would be no defiant haven of its hopes, <br>For now Kindness knew it would forever be of Rularuu.'"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - VileAgreement 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P1224882867" "A Vile Agreement"
// DetailString :
"P2798212786" "The text of this unspeakable pledge is written in blood on what might be vellum. It outlines a deal between the Circle of Thorns and fiendish creatures from the lower levels of existence. In exchange for a promise of human souls and unrestricted access to the Shadow Shard, the demons will help the Oranbegans by moving them to even the most well defended places within the Shadow Shard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - ToBindAGod 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2387945339" "The Tome of Great Binding"
// DetailString :
"P1647117336" "This well-illustrated book is written in the native language of Oranbega, and it's margins are covered in notes. Even without the language, you can tell from the diagrams and symbols that it provides an overview on how one could bind beings of incredible power, and use their vast might as a source of mystic energy. Though from what you can tell the book itself is rather abstract, the hand-written notes on each page contain numerous sketches of the Chantry, it's layout, the surrounding zone, and even Faathim the kind. <br><br>There can be only one conclusion: The Circle of Thorns is planning to capture and bind Faathim himself, and use his power for their own."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode1Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2512368543" "The Trust of Faathim"
// DetailString :
"P1943887376" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode2Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2123273236" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode3Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3817333958" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode4Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1776240838" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode5Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P4012152597" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode6Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2479928343" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode7Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1925724731" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing."

