"P1021192671" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode9Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2703491728" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode10Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P3503467680" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns! <br><br>You then got more recordings of the monument in the Bastion of Sorrow for Augustine to Translate."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode11Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1776793643" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns! <br><br>You then got more recordings of the monument in the Bastion of Sorrow for Augustine to Translate. <br><br>With Faathim's next task translated, you battled the Circle of Thorns again. This time, they had been kidnapping Shadow Shard natives for some dire purpose."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode12Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P2137710111" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns! <br><br>You then got more recordings of the monument in the Bastion of Sorrow for Augustine to Translate. <br><br>With Faathim's next task translated, you battled the Circle of Thorns again. This time, they had been kidnapping Shadow Shard natives for some dire purpose. <br><br>You got the translation of the last monument in the Bastion of Regret."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode13Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// DetailString :
"P1818802370" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns! <br><br>You then got more recordings of the monument in the Bastion of Sorrow for Augustine to Translate. <br><br>With Faathim's next task translated, you battled the Circle of Thorns again. This time, they had been kidnapping Shadow Shard natives for some dire purpose. <br><br>You got the translation of the last monument in the Bastion of Regret. <br><br>You went to speak with Faathim the Kind, only to have him confirm that yes, he was or is one of the Rularuu, but that he rebelled against them. He asked you to help him protect the natives of the Shard by battling the Circle of Thorns."

