// DetailString :
"P3614153833" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns! <br><br>You then got more recordings of the monument in the Bastion of Sorrow for Augustine to Translate. <br><br>With Faathim's next task translated, you battled the Circle of Thorns again. This time, they had been kidnapping Shadow Shard natives for some dire purpose. <br><br>You got the translation of the last monument in the Bastion of Regret. <br><br>You went to speak with Faathim the Kind, only to have him confirm that yes, he was or is one of the Rularuu, but that he rebelled against them. He asked you to help him protect the natives of the Shard by battling the Circle of Thorns. <br><br>You battled the Circle, and found that they had captured more people to sacrifice to demons. In exchange, the demons would move the Circle between Earth and the Shadow Shard."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue - Episode14Clue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Clue Name :
"P2751465128" "The Chantry Under Seige"
// DetailString :
"P2973907125" "Justin Augustine, a mystic researcher and ritual wizard, asked for your help in his ongoing investigation into the Chantry. You started by fighting the Rularuu around the Path of Tears. <br><br> You next travelled to the island group called the 'Bastion of Pain', and after battleing the Rularuu, you took recordings of the monument back to Augustine, who was able to translate them. <br><br>You next got recordings or the monument on the Bastion of Denial for Augustine, and received that translation. <br><br>You fought the Rularuu and got recordings from the monument on the Bastion of Guilt, and got the translation from Augustine. <br><br>With three translations complete, you went to speak with Faathim the Kind himself, the master of the Chantry. Faathim encouraged your efforts, and also gave you a list of tasks that you might be interested in in languages that Augustine could translate. <br><br>The first of Faathim's task was to battle the Rularuu around the path of Rage. When you returned, Augustine had learned more of the language by the translating Faathim's tasks. <br><br>You next helped Dr. Bruce Boyd by gathering more records of Monuments around Firebase Zulu. With what Augustine had learned of the language and passed on to him, Dr. Boyd was able to translate more of the mysterious writing. <br><br>You next got recordings of another monument on the Bastion of Shame, which Augustine translated. <br><br>You next handled one of Faathim's task to root out 'Interlopers' in the caverns of the Bastion of Guilt. These 'Interlopers' proved to be the Circle of Thorns! <br><br>You then got more recordings of the monument in the Bastion of Sorrow for Augustine to Translate. <br><br>With Faathim's next task translated, you battled the Circle of Thorns again. This time, they had been kidnapping Shadow Shard natives for some dire purpose. <br><br>You got the translation of the last monument in the Bastion of Regret. <br><br>You went to speak with Faathim the Kind, only to have him confirm that yes, he was or is one of the Rularuu, but that he rebelled against them. He asked you to help him protect the natives of the Shard by battling the Circle of Thorns. <br><br>You battled the Circle, and found that they had captured more people to sacrifice to demons. In exchange, the demons would move the Circle between Earth and the Shadow Shard. <br><br>Finally, you found out the Circle's plan: To magically bind Faathim the Kind, and use his power for their own evil ends. You arrived to late to stop them before they launched their attack, and now will have to battle them within the Chantry."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// SouvenirClueDef - SL9_TaskForceAugustine_SouvenirClue 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// tDetailString :
"P892850618" "Through your work and perseverence, you were able to uncover the Saga of Faathim. In it's proper order, it reads: <br><br>'And give over your strong to Ruladak that he may work them, <br>And give over your injuries to Faathim that he may heal them, <br>And give over your outcast to Lanaru that he may execute them, <br>For you will know that they are Rularuu and are to be obeyed. <br><br>And Faathim formed the Chantry from the very air, <br>And Faathim alone was master of it, <br>And within the Chantry Faathim stood shielded from Rularuu's will, <br>Here Faathim schemed for his freedom and his oblivion. <br><br>And by word and trickery the Traitor Faathim's work was done, <br>And the Mad One rose up with rage to split the world asunder, <br>And the Rularuu lost their truth and the People their master, <br>For Faathim's betrayal hid all from Rularuu's power. <br><br>And when the world was split the Strong one Remained Loyal, <br>And the Strong one called Faathim Traitor for his plans, <br>And the Strong One called Faathim Traitor for his actions, <br>For Strength would let none stray from Rularuu. 'And Kindness and Strength shook the the world with battle, <br>And by clever stratagem Strength was caught and bound, <br>And Kindness was was trapped as well within it's fortress, <br>While Madness burned with rage and battled all. <br><br>And the Kind One was made prisoner within his Chantry,<br>And the Rularuu beset him in unending siege, <br>And Faathim the Kind knew only anguish, <br>For all his plans were cast down in ruin. <br><br>And Kindness knew there would be freedom, <br>And Kindness knew that Rularuu could not be overthrown, <br>And Kindness new there would be no defiant haven of its hopes, <br>For now Kindness knew it would forever be of Rularuu.' <br><br>In the course of discovering Faathim's history, you learned of a plot against him by the Circle of Thorns. You foiled their plans to bind the Kind One, and gained the Trust of Faathim the Kind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_KillTask1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P560932075" "All right, {TaskForceName}, it's time to get on with what this is all about. Far out in the center of this region is a place called the Chantry. It's supposed to hold all kinds of vast and ancient secrets, including a powerful being the natives only refer to as 'The Kind One'. Now, a title like that can mean a lot of things in folklore, like trying to placate something monstrous. I think the key to understanding a lot of this place is going to be understanding the truth behind the Chantry and what's inside it. And for that, I need your help."
// AcceptString :
"P44902644" "Begin the investigation into the Chantry"
// SendOffString :
"P1163519850" "Alright, before I send you deep into the islands around here, first order of business is to secure this position some. I've managed to keep the Rularuu from finding me here, but they're going to notice you lot coming and going. So, I want you to lower their numbers around the Path of Tears. Take out about 50 or so, that should put a dent in them."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3257315815" "Battle Rularuu in Path of Tears"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P3708040676" "You'll have to take out about 50 Rularuu around the Path of Tears. You can handle it."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1270786636" "Rularuu!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P660670500" "You have defeated enough of the Rularuu to secure the area"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1748910632" "Now that the Rularuu are a little less unruly, it's time to start the real work."
// RandomFameString :
"P1629728550" "I've heard that {HeroName} has joined a special group called {TaskForceName} for some big secret mission."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3609163144" "Time to do some investigation. {TaskFoceName}, I'll need you lot to to go to one of the island groups in here. It's called the Bastion of Pain, and it's the closest cluster of islands to where we are now. There's a monument there I'd like you to take a good look at, and get me some close-up photos."
// AcceptString :
"P380265579" "Travel to Bastion of Pain"
// SendOffString :
"P399238873" "This one's a two parter. First, you'll need to fight the Rularuu around the Bastion of Pain. Once you've fought enough to keep them from interfering,   go to the monument and record it for me. I think I'll be able to translate it. That might tell us something about what's really going on here."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound2_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3601267420" "Battle on Bastion of Pain"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2892968165" "After you've cleared out enough of the Rularuu, you'll need to get to the monument. But you gotta handle the Rularuu first."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P2102224713" "Rularuu! Kill!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P193063322" "You have defeated enough of the Rularuu around the Bastion of Pain"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound2_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P1123182127" "Visit Monument of Pain"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1161924753" "Now that the Rularuu are a bit more under control, you should be able to get to the monument."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1208722978" "You have been to the Monument of Pain, and made records of it for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P227839472" "Thanks for that one. You're all as good as gold. Now, give me a minute. This is very weird stuff. <br><br>Like trying to read Sumerian written with Aztec grammar and English slang. <br><br>I can give you a rough translation of this one, but we're gonna need to see more. Roughly, it would go: <br><br>'And the Kind One was made prisoner within his Chantry,<br>And the Rularuu beset him in unending siege, <br>And Faathim the Kind knew only anguish, <br>For all his plans were cast down in ruin.' <br><br>Pretty heavy stuff, but it still doesn't tell us a lot. There's got to be more to this story."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound3 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2430877174" "The first monument you looked at on the Bastion of Pain seemed to be telling part of a story. The others may have more of it. I'd like you to travel to the Bastion of Denial, clear out some of the Rularuu, and take a look at the monument there. It may have more of this story, or at least help what we have to make sense."
// AcceptString :
"P3289144268" "Travel to Bastion of Denial"
// SendOffString :
"P4262656223" "This one's another two parter. Same set-up as the last one. You'll need to fight the Rularuu around the Bastion of Denial to get them off-balance, then get to the monument and take some recordings and stuff for me. Easy for you, I'm sure."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound3_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P2017402364" "Battle on Bastion of Denial"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P2942038057" "{TaskForceName}! Kill!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1520593286" "You have defeated enough of the Rularuu around the Bastion of Denial"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound3_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3189236921" "Visit Monument of Denial"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P439424337" "You have been to the Monument of Denial, and made records of it for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1099939454" "Great job, all of you. Let me take a look at this. <br>These are getting harder to understand. I could swear that's greek, but that bit there looks like cuneiform, and I don't even know what that last bit is. <br>Okay, here's my best go: <br><br>'And Faathim formed the Chantry from the very air, <br>And Faathim alone was master of it, <br>And within the Chantry Faathim stood shielded from Rularuu's will, <br>Here Faathim schemed for his freedom and his oblivion' <br><br>I'm not completely sure that's right, but it's at least close. I think. We need to find out more."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound4 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3628334146" "The first two monuments seemed to be telling part of a story, but we only have pieces of it. They're getting harder to translate, but we'll have to see what we can get from the next one, in the Bastion of Guilt."
// AcceptString :
"P3116536064" "Travel to Bastion of Guilt"
// SendOffString :
"P3206014432" "You lot should have this set-up down by now. First thing to do is clear out some of the Rularuu, then get recordings of the monument for me. I'll see what I can do to translate them, and we'll go from there."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound4_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3959929777" "Battle on Bastion of Guilt"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P3623730887" "Slay! Murder! Rularuu!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1936029703" "You have defeated enough of the Rularuu around the Bastion of Guilt"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound4_Part2 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3358018699" "Visit Monument of Guilt"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3640509403" "You have been to the Monument of Guilt, and made records of it for Justin Augustine"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3093994129" "Great work, all, these are the best yet. Not too sure how much good it will be, though. I'm able to recognize less and less of this. Let me see if I can get anything. <br><br>Alright, I'll give it a bash, but I can't promise that this is anything close to accurate: <br><br>'And when the world was split the Strong one Remained Loyal, <br>And the Strong one called Faathim Traitor for his plans, <br>And the Strong One called Faathim Traitor for his actions, <br>For Strength would let none stray from Rularuu' <br><br>I'm not that confidant about that, but it's the best I can do. At least I think I know what the next step's going to have to be."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_DeliverTask5 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2293818910" "I've done about all the translating that can be done without a better knowledge of the languages used. So, now's the time to try and find out more about the whole thing right from the source. {TaskForceName}, I need you to go into the Chantry itself and talk to Faathim the Kind."
// AcceptString :
"P238464776" "Enter the Chantry proper and speak with Faathim the Kind"
// SendOffString :
"P4089199619" "The good news is I don't think Faathim will be out-right hostile. Bad news, of course, is that there's a lot of things surrounding the entrance who probably will be hostile."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P898282097" "Speak to Faathim"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P97554244" "You need to fight or sneak your way in and talk to Faathim. Or speed past, or teleport if you can make it. Probably ain't gonna be easy any way you try."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1730775438" "{TaskForceName} knows too much."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3705276306" "I am Faathim, called the Kind one. You are all welcome before me, members of {TaskForceName}. I have watched you from within my Chantry, and I know what you seek. I will tell you that you have learned nothing untrue or false. <br><br>I am the master of the Chantry, <br>and I am its prisoner, <br>and I am a traitor above all. <br>But there is more than those three elements. I will provide you with this. It is a series of tasks that need the attention of heroes, and it is written in languages that Justin Augustine will understand. Your reward shall be righteousness in your work, and furtherance of your knowledge. <br><br>I ask only this: You must remember that something learned cannot be unlearned, and nothing can ever be undone."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P1603069126" "Glad to hear you got such a welcome reception, if a bit on the cryptic side. Still, this list of Faathim's could be very useful. Give me a bit, I'll see what I can get out of this."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_KillTask6 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1061251276" "I've been able to translate some of this list of 'Heroic Deeds' Faathim gave you. First one sounds like something you can handle. It's a request to battle the Rularuu down around the Path of Rage near the Chantry. Might be a good idea to do it at that."
// AcceptString :
"P1400387643" "Battle the Rularuu around the Path of Rage"
// SendOffString :
"P4022878759" "I'm not sure exactly what Faathim the Kind wants with this task, but it seems pretty innocuous. While you're working on that, I'm going to look back over my notes with what I've learned from translating the first part of this."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P3815033609" "Battle Rularuu in Path of Rage"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P2631948243" "You'll have to take out about 50 Rularuu around the Path of Rage. I don't know why Faathim the Kind wants that done, but it seems pretty innocuous."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P4212636651" "You have defeated enough of the Rularuu to complete Faathim's first mission"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P793690978" "All right, now that I've had a bit of time, I think I may have made a breakthrough on this. It might shed light on a lot of things we've found already. How would you all like to take a vist back to Fire Base Zulu?"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound7 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P3060745256" "Just translating the list of tasks Faathim gave you is teaching me a lot about the languages used here. In fact, some of what I've learned may be very useful to some of the other people working in the Shard. I've been communicating with Dr. Boyd, over in the Firebase Zulu area. He thinks he might be on the verge of a breakthrough in his own translations due to this new information, but he's going to need some help. While I'm working on translating more of Faathim's list, how about you lot go over and lend him a hand?"
// AcceptString :
"P2988361294" "Help Dr. Boyd in Firebase Zulu"
// SendOffString :
"P3756241934" "Thanks. I hope that Dr. Boyd's work will shed some light on my own. The more I understand, the stranger this gets."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_Compound7_Part1 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// ActiveTaskString :
"P493668040" "Meet with Dr. Boyd"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1376738244" "Dr. Boyd's waiting to meet you over at Point Echo around Firebase Zulu."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P1420845193" "Hunt {TaskForceName}!"

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3119472414" "Ah! Hello there! So, this would be the illustrious {TaskForceName}, eh? Goodgoodgood. Now, I've asked for your assistance for two major things. First, with the new translations by Mr. Augustine we're getting closer to understanding what these amazing monuments may really mean. That's really the trick you see: Meaning. They have different levels of them. The monuments, I mean. We already know something about them, but that's like knowing a bit about nuclear engineering. Don't want to go building a reactor when you haven't gotten to the chapter on cooling systems. With some of the powerful beings reported out here, well, you get the analogy. So, I need new, fresh records of several Monuments around the area. Many of them were damaged at some time in the past, so getting close-up images is vital. Which was the second thing. The, ah, Rularuu have gotten very agitated about my work recently, which is the other reason I requested your aid. Be on the lookout for them."

