// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2466794552" "Alright. Let me have a bash at this. These are getting almost easy. <br><br>'And Kindness knew there would be freedom, <br>And Kindness knew that Rularuu could not be overthrown, <br>And Kindness new there would be no defiant haven of its hopes, <br>For now Kindness knew it would forever be of Rularuu.' <br><br>Right... <br><br>I think you need to talk to Faathim the Kind."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SL9_TFA_DeliverTask13 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P2431839926" "From what we've gathered from the monuments, there's a lot of background that Faathim the Kind hasn't been telling us. If he's really part of the Rularuu, whether he betrayed them before or not, we need to know. I don't think this is going to be a fight, but you'll still have to get past all of the stuff outside the Chantry."
// SendOffString :
"P2168111708" "Once you get in there, ask Faathim about what the monuments say. Be ready for anything, but I don't think it's going to come down to a fight."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - VILLAIN_GROUP 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Variable - LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// LOITER_ATTACK_TEXT :
"P4200090500" "It is too late to interfere, {TaskForceName}."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - TaskComplete 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3210227362" "You have done well to find this out. I will place it in order for you, and give it to you to know. <br><br>You ask me if I am part of the Rularuu? I tell you then that I am Rularuu, but Rularuu is more than just my one fragmentary self. <br>I am of  Rularuu, and that is my crime, and that is my shame, and that is the reason I made my rebellion. I had felt the first portals from your world, and hoped perhaps to make a place where explorers would be welcome. I sought to build a place of peace, I sought to build a haven from Rularuu's power. I erred, and I failed. Not in my action, but in its execution. I did not realize what strength had been trapped here when the madness broke the world. I have received my punishment, and I remain in my prison. <br><br>My crimes are past, and my concern is for the descendants of those I was unable to provide a true shelter for. I know now that the interlopers of the Green Eyed Cult draw new plans against those innocent people. Their final end is unknown to me, but it is wicked and will cause much pain. I now ask you heroes to move against them. I ask you to battle them, and to save the lives of the people they have taken before those lives are lost."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P3599256725" "I love the way big mystical muckity-mucks can answer all your questions without explaining a thing. What does that mean, he 'is Rularuu but Rularuu is more than him'? At least he copped to it. If he was really trying to hide it he could get us to work for them, he wouldn't just come out and say what he was, would he? Still not sure I get the whole thing, and I don't know if I trust Faathim, but I can tell you that his list of tasks is probably still worth doing, no matter Faathim's motivation. The Circle need to be stopped."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

