// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Dialog :
"P2352858651" "That sick pact you found explains what the Circle have been up to with all of the captives, but I almost wish I didn't know. How many people have they sacrificed to the demons already? Their final aim, whatever it is, has got to be stopped. And here's the funny bit. The second to last item of Faathim's list is in Oranbega."

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Reward - ReturnSuccess 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task - SF9_TFA_Mission15 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Task Header Items 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// IntroString :
"P1663914135" "Faathim's second to last task is against the Circle of Thorns in Oranbega. It's going to be up to you to put an end to whatever plan they had. We know that they were sacrificing shard natives to Demons in order to cross the dimensional barriers. We also know that they could reach even the furthest and most well defended parts of the Shadow Shard. The only thing we don't know is why. I just hope we can find an answer down in Oranbega."
// AcceptString :
"P3598434935" "Defeat the Circle's plans in Oranbega"
// SendOffString :
"P1861366664" "Your goal here is to find and take out whoever was leading this operation. Hopefully, that will be enough to shut it down before they can complete whatever hellish objective they have."
// ActiveTaskString :
"P4223297256" "Defeat Circle leaders"
// YoureStillBusyString :
"P1090037413" "You have to defeat the Circle members in charge of this whole plan before they can finish it."

